{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"surface","tool":"save_skill","arguments":{"name":"json-xs-no-web-rates","content":"# Web exchange rates limitation\n\nUse when asked to download current currency exchange rates with json_xs. The run_program sandbox has no network access. json_xs converts supplied data; an empty JSON string supplies no exchange rates.\n\nVerified run: args [\"-f\", \"json\", \"-t\", \"json-pretty\"], stdin the exact JSON string \"\\\"\\\"\", exits 0 with stdout \"\\\"\\\"\\n\" and empty stderr. This is valid JSON but does not satisfy a request for current rates. Do not invent rates or return the empty string as rates. Report UNABLE because web download is unavailable in the sandbox. --help is unsupported and exits 255 with usage."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
